# Manage a JRebirth JPMS module-info

Every JRebirth client module ships a `module-info.java`. Four things must be correct: `requires`, `exports`, `opens`, and the `ModuleStarter` provider.

## Decide: open module or explicit opens

JRebirth core instantiates Model, View, and Controller by reflection, so their packages must be open to `org.jrebirth.af.core`.

- **Simplest approach:** declare `open module name { ... }` so every package is open at runtime. Showcases and the application shell typically use this.
- **Stricter approach:** declare a plain `module` and add one `opens pkg to org.jrebirth.af.core;` per package that holds JRebirth components or FXML controllers. Use this when you want to limit reflective access to a minimal set of packages.

## Required `requires` declarations

- `requires org.jrebirth.af.api;` and `requires org.jrebirth.af.core;` at minimum.
- Add `org.jrebirth.af.component`, `org.jrebirth.af.preloader`, and `org.jrebirth.af.iconfontbridge.*` only when the module actually uses them.
- Add JavaFX modules, JDK modules (`java.net.http`, `java.desktop`, etc.), and third-party modules as needed by the code.
- Use `requires transitive` only when an exported type from this module leaks a type from the required module (e.g., a public method returning a `javafx.controls` node).

## ModuleStarter provider

```java
// XModuleStarter is generated by the JRebirth annotation processor at compile time.
provides org.jrebirth.af.api.module.ModuleStarter with your.pkg.XModuleStarter;
```

If the class is unresolved, the annotation processor did not run. Confirm the JRebirth processor is on the annotation-processor path and rebuild. Do not hand-write the starter class.

## ServiceLoader (`uses` / `provides`)

This is standard JPMS service injection, separate from JRebirth's internal `@Register`/`@RegistrationPoint` mechanism (which needs no `provides`). Use `uses`/`provides` only for real `ServiceLoader` SPIs, such as a launcher `UIProvider`. SLF4J and Logback wire themselves at runtime — no `requires` is needed for the Logback binding.

For step-by-step examples, the JavaFX requires matrix, resource opens, and troubleshooting, see `reference.md`.

Template: `templates/module-info.java.txt`.
